773 silly install resolved       '## Motivation\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'Instead of implementing `XMLHttpRequest` in Node.js to run browser-specific [Fetch polyfill](https://github.com/github/fetch), why not go from native `http` to `fetch` API directly? Hence, `node-fetch`, minimal code for a `window.fetch` compatible API on Node.js runtime.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "See Matt Andrews' [isomorphic-fetch](https://github.com/matthew-andrews/isomorphic-fetch) or Leonardo Quixada's [cross-fetch](https://github.com/lquixada/cross-fetch) for isomorphic usage (exports `node-fetch` for server-side, `whatwg-fetch` for client-side).\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '## Features\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '- Stay consistent with `window.fetch` API.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '- Make conscious trade-off when following [WHATWG fetch spec][whatwg-fetch] and [stream spec](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/) implementation details, document known differences.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '- Use native promise but allow substituting it with [insert your favorite promise library].\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '- Use native Node streams for body on both request and response.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '- Decode content encoding (gzip/deflate) properly and convert string output (such as `res.text()` and `res.json()`) to UTF-8 automatically.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '- Useful extensions such as timeout, redirect limit, response size limit, [explicit errors](ERROR-HANDLING.md) for troubleshooting.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '## Difference from client-side fetch\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '- See [Known Differences](LIMITS.md) for details.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '- If you happen to use a missing feature that `window.fetch` offers, feel free to open an issue.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '- Pull requests are welcomed too!\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '## Installation\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'Current stable release (`2.x`)\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```sh\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '$ npm install node-fetch\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '## Loading and configuring the module\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'We suggest you load the module via `require` until the stabilization of ES modules in node:\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "const fetch = require('node-fetch');\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'If you are using a Promise library other than native, set it through `fetch.Promise`:\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "const Bluebird = require('bluebird');\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'fetch.Promise = Bluebird;\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '## Common Usage\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'NOTE: The documentation below is up-to-date with `2.x` releases; see the [`1.x` readme](https://github.com/bitinn/node-fetch/blob/1.x/README.md), [changelog](https://github.com/bitinn/node-fetch/blob/1.x/CHANGELOG.md) and [2.x upgrade guide](UPGRADE-GUIDE.md) for the differences.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '#### Plain text or HTML\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://github.com/')\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => res.text())\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(body => console.log(body));\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '#### JSON\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://api.github.com/users/github')\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => res.json())\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(json => console.log(json));\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '#### Simple Post\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://httpbin.org/post', { method: 'POST', body: 'a=1' })\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => res.json()) // expecting a json response\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(json => console.log(json));\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '#### Post with JSON\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'const body = { a: 1 };\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://httpbin.org/post', {\n" +
773 silly install resolved       "        method: 'post',\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '        body:    JSON.stringify(body),\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '    })\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => res.json())\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(json => console.log(json));\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '#### Post with form parameters\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '`URLSearchParams` is available in Node.js as of v7.5.0. See [official documentation](https://nodejs.org/api/url.html#url_class_urlsearchparams) for more usage methods.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'NOTE: The `Content-Type` header is only set automatically to `x-www-form-urlencoded` when an instance of `URLSearchParams` is given as such:\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "const { URLSearchParams } = require('url');\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'const params = new URLSearchParams();\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "params.append('a', 1);\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://httpbin.org/post', { method: 'POST', body: params })\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => res.json())\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(json => console.log(json));\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '#### Handling exceptions\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'NOTE: 3xx-5xx responses are *NOT* exceptions and should be handled in `then()`; see the next section for more information.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'Adding a catch to the fetch promise chain will catch *all* exceptions, such as errors originating from node core libraries, network errors and operational errors, which are instances of FetchError. See the [error handling document](ERROR-HANDLING.md)  for more details.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://domain.invalid/')\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '    .catch(err => console.error(err));\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '#### Handling client and server errors\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'It is common to create a helper function to check that the response contains no client (4xx) or server (5xx) error responses:\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'function checkStatus(res) {\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    if (res.ok) { // res.status >= 200 && res.status < 300\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '        return res;\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    } else {\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '        throw MyCustomError(res.statusText);\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    }\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '}\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://httpbin.org/status/400')\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(checkStatus)\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "    .then(res => console.log('will not get here...'))\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '## Advanced Usage\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '#### Streams\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'The "Node.js way" is to use streams when possible:\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "fetch('https://assets-cdn.github.com/images/modules/logos_page/Octocat.png')\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '    .then(res => {\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "        const dest = fs.createWriteStream('./octocat.png');\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '        res.body.pipe(dest);\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    });\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'In Node.js 14 you can also use async iterators to read `body`; however, be careful to catch\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'errors -- the longer a response runs, the more likely it is to encounter an error.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "const fetch = require('node-fetch');\n" +
773 silly install resolved       "const response = await fetch('https://httpbin.org/stream/3');\n" +
773 silly install resolved       'try {\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\tfor await (const chunk of response.body) {\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\t\tconsole.dir(JSON.parse(chunk.toString()));\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\t}\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '} catch (err) {\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\tconsole.error(err.stack);\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '}\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'In Node.js 12 you can also use async iterators to read `body`; however, async iterators with streams\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'did not mature until Node.js 14, so you need to do some extra work to ensure you handle errors\n' +
773 silly install resolved       'directly from the stream and wait on it response to fully close.\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '```js\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "const fetch = require('node-fetch');\n" +
773 silly install resolved       'const read = async body => {\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    let error;\n' +
773 silly install resolved       "    body.on('error', err => {\n" +
773 silly install resolved       '        error = err;\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    });\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '    for await (const chunk of body) {\n' +
773 silly install resolved       '        console.dir(JSON.parse(chunk.toString()));\n' +
